# load module (opt-in: add "load" to [FERRUM]MODULES in ferrum.ini).
# ferrum.load.value is a float input, 0 (idle) to 1 (full load). The
# backplot colours the tool's trail by it: green, amber, red, and each
# program run's load is recorded (docs/ferrum-toml.md, Cutting load records).
#
# Nothing is netted yet: the mill has no load signal. When one exists, scale
# it to 0..1 here and net it, for example:
#   net spindle-load-fraction => ferrum.load.value
